    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2e0734d54dd2cac2341a57b109f12156431d6469568939967ffb816ef6378c7b",
      "text": "Bonito is one of Brazil’s best-known ecotourism destinations. Forests surround caves with stalactites and stalagmites, waterfalls and clear rivers teeming with fish.\n\nAfter breakfast, visit Blue Lake Cave, known for its rock formations and vivid sky-blue water. Sunlight reaches into the grotto and lights up the water. It is among the world’s large flooded caves.\n\nIn 1992, a team of Brazilian palaeontologists discovered the fossilised remains of prehistoric mammals on the cave floor, including a giant sloth and a sabre-toothed cat.\n\nAfter lunch, the programme takes you into the waters of the Rio da Prata. Visibility reaches about 50 metres in the clear river, making it easy to see fish and aquatic plants.\n\nFirst, follow a trail through the reserve along the Rio da Prata. Then reach the Olho d’Água spring, where the float down the river begins. As you swim, you may see golden-coloured fish, piraputangas and pacus. Masks and the necessary equipment are provided at the reserve.\n\nOvernight at a hotel in Bonito.",
      "provenance": {
